course: dictionary
lesson: 6435
title: Myths and facts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A myth is a story or an idea that many people believe but that is not true. Some myths are very old tales about gods, heroes and magical creatures, such as Zeus, Thor or Maui, which explain things like thunder or the seasons. Other myths are modern ideas that people repeat until they seem true.
explain: Context helps you spot which kind you are reading. «The old saying "feed a cold, starve a fever" is a myth.» The sentence tells you the saying is not true. Try the swap test: put "a true idea" in place of myth. Does the sentence still make sense? If not, your meaning is wrong.
explain: «A girl in Kansas hears in a video that a drop of bleach in water cures colds; her mum explains that it is a dangerous myth.» Here the myth is a false idea that could hurt someone. Clues like "dangerous" and "explains" show that it is not true, and that checking is a good thing to do.
fact: A myth is a very old story about gods, heroes or magical creatures.
fact: A myth is also a common idea that many people believe but that is not true.
fact: «That's a myth» means it isn't true.
fact: «Myth-busting» means checking popular ideas to show they are false, such as the idea that goldfish have three-second memories.
fact: Checking facts helps you spot myths.
exercise: «The old saying "feed a cold, starve a fever" is a myth.» What does myth mean here? | A very old story about the god Thor | A rule that must always be followed | A kind of fever | *A common idea that is not true
exercise: Which of these is a myth from long ago? | Bread is made with flour | *The story of Thor, the Norse god of thunder | The Earth goes round the Sun once every year | Water boils at 100 degrees Celsius
exercise: «Educated people in Columbus's time already knew the Earth was round, so the story that he proved it is a myth.» Why is the story a myth? | Because the Earth is flat | *Because people already knew the Earth was round, so he did not prove it | Because Columbus was a famous gardener | Because it is a story about a dragon
test: «A girl in Kansas hears in a video that a drop of bleach in water cures colds; her mum explains that it is a dangerous myth.» What is the dangerous myth? | *That bleach in water cures colds | That videos are always true | That mums are always right | That Kansas is in Canada
test: What is the best way to check whether an idea is a myth? | *Check the facts with a trusted source | Believe whatever most people say | Only trust what you see in a video | Ask an adult and say it must be true
exam: Mia says a myth is only a story from long ago. Is she right? | Yes, myths are always true | Yes, only old stories are myths | *No, a myth can also be a common idea that many people believe but is not true | No, myths are always about dinosaurs
